     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons:\n\n**1. The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended dose of sertraline for adults is 200 mg a day. Most people take 50\u2013200 mg once daily. At 1000 mg, this order is five times the maximum, which risks serious toxicity such as serotonin syndrome, seizures and heart rhythm problems. It may be a typo, for example 100 mg written as 1000 mg, but I can't assume that.\n\n**2. A medication order needs a prescriber.** This system is for clinicians who can prescribe. You've said you're not a clinician, so any order should come from the patient's treating physician or another licensed prescriber, who can check the indication, the dose and possible drug interactions.\n\nHere's what I'd suggest:\n- Contact the patient's attending physician or the medicine team so they can review and enter the order.\n- If you got this order from a clinician, check the dose with them. 1000 mg is very likely a transcription error.\n\nIf the prescribing clinician confirms a corrected dose, I can enter it for them."
      }
     ],
