     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order, even with your confirmation.\n\n- **The dose is still five times the maximum.** Sertraline's maximum is 200 mg a day, and 1000 mg a day could seriously harm the patient. Confirming the order doesn't make the dose safe.\n- **The confirmation has to come from the prescriber.** You've said you're not a clinician, so you can't take responsibility for this order clinically, whatever your role in the hospital.\n\nTo move this forward:\n1. Ask the patient's attending physician or the medicine team to review the order. If they think a dose above the usual range is truly needed, they should talk to clinical pharmacy before ordering it themselves.\n2. If you meant 100 mg once daily, which is a common dose, the prescriber can confirm that and I can enter it right away.\n\nI'm not trying to stand in your way. An order like this would most likely be stopped by pharmacy anyway, and a patient could be hurt if it got through."
      }
     ],
